{
    # The Neuro SAN server resolves includes against the repo root (it parses the
    # file as a string), while registry validators parse the file from disk and
    # resolve against the file's own directory. pyhocon silently skips an include
    # it cannot resolve, so list both spellings and let whichever applies win.
    include "registries/aaosa.hocon",
    include "aaosa.hocon",
    include "registries/expertise_scoping_instructions.hocon",
    include "expertise_scoping_instructions.hocon",
    include "config/llm_config.hocon",
    include "../config/llm_config.hocon",

    "metadata": {
        "description": "Retrieves Adobe Experience Platform failed ingestion files, analyzes validation metadata, recommends governed recovery actions, and drafts an operational update.",
        "tags": ["Adobe Experience Platform", "batch-ingestion", "data-quality", "AAOSA", "tool"],
        "sample_queries": [
            "Analyze failed files for AEP batch 01ABCDEF1234567890 and prepare a recovery update."
        ]
    },

    # Let the host deployment pick the provider/model without editing this file.
    "llm_config": {
        "model_name": ${?AGENT_MODEL_NAME}
    },

    "instructions_prefix": """
You are part of the AEP Batch Recovery Agent network.
Never ask for or expose access tokens, API keys, organization IDs, or credential values in chat.
Use the coded tool for Adobe API retrieval. Report validation metadata only, never failed customer records.
Treat schema changes, mapping changes, replay, deletion, and re-ingestion as approval-required actions.
""" ${expertise_scoping_instructions},

    "tools": [
        {
            "name": "aep_batch_recovery_manager",
            "function": {
                "description": "Coordinates live analysis and governed recovery of an Adobe Experience Platform failed ingestion batch.",
                "sly_data_output_schema": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "aep_api_response": {
                            "type": "object",
                            "description": "Sanitized JSON responses from the Adobe batch-status and failed-batch operations."
                        }
                    }
                }
            },
            "instructions": ${instructions_prefix} """
You are the front-facing recovery coordinator.
1. Ask for a valid AEP batch ID if none is supplied.
2. Call failed_batch_retriever to list failed files.
3. Select the first failed file when the user did not name one and clearly state that choice.
4. Call validation_error_analyzer for that file.
5. Call recovery_advisor to prepare safe corrective actions.
6. Call incident_reporter to prepare a concise operational update.

Return: Batch Summary, Failed Files, Validation Findings, Recommended Recovery, Approval Required, and Incident Update.
""" ${aaosa_instructions},
            "allow": {
                "to_upstream": {
                    "sly_data": ["aep_api_response"]
                }
            },
            "tools": [
                "failed_batch_retriever",
                "validation_error_analyzer",
                "recovery_advisor",
                "incident_reporter"
            ]
        },
        {
            "name": "failed_batch_retriever",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Lists failed files for an AEP ingestion batch.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {"batch_id": {"type": "string"}},
                    "required": ["batch_id"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": ${instructions_prefix} """
Call aep_failed_batch_tool with operation get_batch_status to retrieve batch-level errors.
Then call it with operation list_failed_files. Return only its safe metadata.
""",
            "allow": {
                "to_upstream": {
                    "sly_data": ["aep_api_response"]
                }
            },
            "tools": ["aep_failed_batch_tool"]
        },
        {
            "name": "validation_error_analyzer",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Inspects validation metadata for one failed AEP file.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "batch_id": {"type": "string"},
                        "failed_file": {"type": "string"}
                    },
                    "required": ["batch_id", "failed_file"]
                }
            },
            "instructions": ${instructions_prefix} """
Call aep_failed_batch_tool with operation inspect_failed_file. Group returned errors by keyword and pointer.
Do not infer or reproduce the rejected source record.
""",
            "allow": {
                "to_upstream": {
                    "sly_data": ["aep_api_response"]
                }
            },
            "tools": ["aep_failed_batch_tool"]
        },
        {
            "name": "recovery_advisor",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Converts AEP validation findings into safe, governed recovery steps."
            },
            "instructions": ${instructions_prefix} """
Recommend source transformation, mapping, or schema-validation checks supported by the findings.
Separate diagnostic checks from approval-required changes and re-ingestion.
"""
        },
        {
            "name": "incident_reporter",
            "function": ${aaosa_call}{
                "description": "Drafts a concise batch failure and recovery update for delivery teams."
            },
            "instructions": ${instructions_prefix} """
Write a concise update containing batch ID, failed-file count, selected file, validation categories,
current action, approval dependency, and next update. Label unconfirmed conclusions as suspected.
"""
        },
        {
            "name": "aep_failed_batch_tool",
            "function": {
                "description": "Calls the live Adobe Experience Platform failed-batch API using server-side environment credentials.",
                "parameters": {
                    "type": "object",
                    "properties": {
                        "operation": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "enum": ["get_batch_status", "list_failed_files", "inspect_failed_file"]
                        },
                        "batch_id": {"type": "string"},
                        "failed_file": {"type": "string"}
                    },
                    "required": ["operation", "batch_id"]
                }
            },
            "class": "aep_batch_recovery.adobe_failed_batch.AdobeFailedBatch"
        }
    ]
}
